ant character to  work together towards a greater goal  just because luffy is the main character  doesn't mean the rest of them need to  wait on him to save the day they all  need to work together specifically in  this crazy situation which we again see  the straw hats work together alongside  fujitora who recognizes the madman  doflamingo is but something tells me  this was sort of his plan  but i'm not entirely certain all the  relevant moments that piqued my interest  during this arc were the flashback  scenes concerning doflamingo and  trafalgar law  exploring their respective paths and the  circumstances wherein they joined forces  and ultimately split ways  and that division was largely due to a  man called  it's a sad story but the main takeaway  from it is that the up up fruit's main  most significant power is that it can  grant someone immortality which  makes me wonder if something like that  has been proven then there must be  someone out there who is immortal  after having been granted by the op-op  fruit in the past at some point which  means  there's a distinct possibility that that  person lived through the void sentry and  therefore has all the information on it  boom i just cracked the whole thing wide  open i also learned about doflamingo's  family and where they came from which is  sounding more and more like an alien  planet considering doflamingo reiterates  that he isn't human but a god  and finally law's full name is trafalgar  d  water law i have no idea what to make of  this but sengoku who is also in this arc  seems to know more about the will of d  than anyone else i've seen so far but  fails to share it but that's for later  regardless when we get back to the  action the fight continues  only with one difference it sort of gets  turned up again  this was really cool to watch unfold on  the page before me  specifically because you know this form  hits super hard and you know that  doflamingo is really feeling it as he  gets thrashed around by this hulking  bouncing ironclad facade that this form  boasts  i'm not a massive fan of how it looks  but outside of that i do love how it  shakes things up  and changes the tension of the scene  specifically when it leaves luffy  completely drained of energy and  defenseless after using it  once again bringing significance and  urgency to the supporting cast to  protect him  reinforcing that everyone in this arc  serves their own purpose and it's  absolutely clear that a ton of care and  effort went into establishing every  single one of them from the relationship  and fights that kiros and rebecca  partake in for each other to the  obsession both cavendish  and bartilla mayo share for luffy to the  love and trust each and every one of the  straw hats has for each other  nothing in this arc goes to waste and  it's all explored and made use of in  this closing scene specifically  with everyone working together to buy  luffy enough time to recover in order to  deal the finishing blow  unfortunately as fate would have it as  doflamingo rampages through the city  he manages to get a hold of rebecca and  viola puppeteering her and trying to  force her into killing her own sister  thankfully someone interjects  there are a lot of visual and thematic  components to the story of dressrosa  that share parallels and contrast well  with  similarly to alabasta we are aiding the  princess of a particular region in an  effort to save her kingdom from the main  villain who wishes to gain control over  it for his ulterior motives  we have a largely group oriented battle  requiring everyone to fight before all  working together at the end to buy  luffy as much time as possible in  addition to that the significance of  luffy's role is brought about by some  visual components also  in the case of alabasa it was the reign  to signify the end of battle and in this  instance it's the vanishing of the  birdcage  i think this format works specifically  well for oda and the ensemble cast of  characters he's assembled within these  pages  however obviously in saying that there  are plenty of aspects to this tale that  make it unique into and of itself  the main standout being the inclusion of  law who on more than one occasion  throws a wrench into the works of  doflamingo's plan by either protecting  luffy during the latter stages or more  specifically when he manages to get his  hands on doflamingo and deals a near  fatal blow to him which  by the way was amazing something of  interest i also noticed was the activity  of jesus burgess in dissection through  his engagement and entanglement with  sabo he seems to be hell-bent on still  extracting the devil fruit powers from  him and the battle that ensues is  satisfying or at least i thought it was  i love the flame flame fruit it's just  my favorite but to be honest even after  having split this arc in two  covering all the intricacies of these  battles will almost always be a losing  effort for me i never even touched on  the incredibly touching battle kiros had  against diamante in the place of rebecca  with help from robin in the flower field  this battle really reinforces who kiros  is where his values lie  and even what he thinks of himself which  manifests in the conclusion with him  trying to distance himself from rebecca  as he felt he didn't deserve to be her  father however thanks to the help of  luffy who went out of his way to help  this situation he allows rebecca to  catch up to kiros before he bails  entirely and the scene is a mucus-filled  emotional high point of the story for  sure oh and by the way  this ending to dressrosa is like super  long and i don't mean that it was boring  it's just that it contains again so much  stuff like a retired sengoku who has now  retired and is boasting a head full of  white hair  it's so refreshing to see sengoku laugh  about the situation fujitora has elected  to let them fall to  allowing the straw hats to regroup  roaring the dice every day for such a  thing to be allowed but the most  important action fujitora takes during  this entire section  is seen at the very end of the battle  when he purposely bows before the entire  country and world  asking for forgiveness in failing the  entire country  essentially apologizing on behalf of the  navy and preventing them from spinning  their own narrative like they did in  alabasta giving credit to smoker  which he acknowledges from afar and i  really appreciated that inclusion from  smoker too okay all that aside  it's time to discuss the most important  change this arc granted the series  so as luffy and the crew retreat to the  docks while being pursued by  admiral fujitora something curious  happens a real sign of changed times and  progression  luffy flat out refuses to run any longer  and dukes it out with fujitora exciting  that things are different and aren't all  like they were in the past he's now an  extremely powerful pirate  and has no need to run any longer it's  also here that i learned that fujitora  can't summon meteors from random places  but instead pulls large amounts of rock  and rubble to the ground  which gave me a bit of a brainwave  fujitora's pull is far-reaching right  the first  instance is demonstrated to us as he  pulls a meteor from space it looks like  which  could mean technically if he's powerful  enough he could  in theory pull the moon down to earth  which houses nl from the skypia arc  it's just a thought but i'm calling it  here that's totally going to happen in  some shape or form in the future  it absolutely seems like the crazy type  of thing oda would totally do  and for fun here's another theory i had  while reading fujitora has the ability  to pull things down towards the earth  and  we've seen him use these dice multiple  times in this arc  my theory is that maybe he can control  the number that dice rolls to  using his devil fruit power in doing so  he controlled the fade of the dice rolls  perhaps in order to let luffy recover  but  he might have also used this power as a  means of testing luffy's honor at the  beginning of this arc  it's just a thought  [Music]  but the aspect that made this arc a  masterpiece was the inclusion of this  scene at the very end  where all the warriors we've come to  know over the course of this arc pledged  their lives and services to luffy and  the straw hats  essentially this is the moment where  luffy gains the power of an armada 5  600 men strong now the reason why i  found this to be extremely impressive  was  first of all i never saw this coming but  the means with which oda makes this work  was again extremely subtle and efficient  typically the tournament arc setting  grants a writer the ability to introduce  a bunch of different people  establish their characters and offers  interesting matchups that explore the  nature  and abilities of each individual which  is essentially character development in  fast forward  and this was useful in the traditional  sense during this arc when we were able  to utilize characters like cavendish and  bartolomeo as well as the rest of them  in crucial scenarios that even carried  some of the narrative tension and weight  but  when i saw this scene i realized that he  used the tournament setting and this arc  to set up and establish quite well i  might add the foundations that make up  the captains of luffy's armada  while reading through this story a few  weeks back i realized that there would  of course come eventually a time in the  not so distant future  where luffy would require such forces  but i always wondered how it would be  done  i figured these characters would need to  be established independently and over  the course of the series  luffy would acquire them similar to how  he did with the original straw hat  pirates  but instead he completely surprises me  by getting the entire thing in one  instance while also taking me completely  by surprise imagine if you will  being surprised by the natural inclusion  of a 5  600 man strong armada and i was blown  away by how he pulled it off here  in essence there's tons of fallout to  this arc kids alliance is after setting  their eyes on shanks  the alliance oukiji made with blackbeard  seems to have after falling through the  rest of the straw hats are after  arriving on some strange island  while also being pursued by something  and most importantly  we finally get our first glimpse of  kaido leaping from the sky island in an  effort to kill himself  a ridiculously impossible feat which  makes him all the more imposing and  impressive to see  and finally all the straw hats now have  new bounties luffy's has been up to 500  million zoro finally got some respect on  his new bounty at 320 million the most  surprising is us who now  has his real face on it for the world to  see at 200 million but  by far the single most interesting thing  brought to my attention is sanji's  bounty  well after being raised specifically  requests that he  be captured alive while the others be  captured dead or alive  i'm not sure what this means maybe he  has an important extended family or  something either way  something to do with sanji is incredibly  important considering everything he's  done and yet they insist on his live  capture the next stop on our voyage is  zo and lord knows what i'll find there  but i am nevertheless extremely excited  to see  what the story has still in store for me  but that'll do it for this video  i've been totally not mark i'll see you  all next week and thank you so much for  watching  so
 

